# CWL — THE language of the web

Canonical constitution: [`docs/language/CWL-PILLAR-HOME.md`](../../docs/language/CWL-PILLAR-HOME.md)

CWL is not a side format. It is the **canonical web language** for Chrysalis: what a web app *is* (routes, pages, data, UI, effects, honest holes).

| Pillar | Relationship to CWL |
| --- | --- |
| **This repo (`chrysalis-cwl`)** | Owns grammar, RFCs, parser/print, fixtures, versioning |
| **Convert** | Translates origin ↔ WebIR/CWL ↔ emit. Pulls language from here |
| **Secure (Helix)** | Protects with traffic DNA; bridges to CWL when comparing/seeding surface — does not fork the language |

## Rules

- Land language fixes **here first**, then `npm run sync:convert`.
- Prefer `fixtures/language-gold` + RFCs over hub/WISP product smokes as language proof.
- Run `npm run test:language` before claiming done.
- Do not implement Helix firewall features here.
- Do not let convert-only forks become the “real” CWL.
- Judge work as a **language** (spec, fixtures, tooling), not a single customer POC.
